        "case_id": "gp002",
        "category": "golden",
        "question": "What are the main components of an LLM-based agent according to the survey?",
        "answer": "- **Brain** – the core of the agent, built around a large language model that stores memory, performs reasoning, and plans actions. [chunk_2]\n- **Perception** – expands the agent’s sensory input from text to multimodal modalities (text, sound, vision, touch, etc.). [chunk_2]\n- **Action** – enables the agent to produce textual output, use tools, and perform embodied actions to interact with and shape its environment. [chunk_2]\n- **Memory** – a subsystem within the brain that records past observations, thoughts, and actions to support strategy formulation and decision‑making. [chunk_5]\n- **Reasoning & Planning** – capabilities of the brain that allow the agent to analyze information and generate high‑level action plans, often enhanced by external feedback or hierarchical reinforcement learning. [chunk_4]",
