        "category": "golden",
        "question": "What is the role of the brain in an LLM-based agent?",
        "answer": "- The brain is the core component of an LLM‑based agent, built around a large language model and serving as the central “control center.” [chunk_1][chunk_2]\n- It stores the agent’s crucial memories, information, and knowledge. [chunk_1]\n- It carries out information‑processing functions such as thinking, decision‑making, reasoning, and planning. [chunk_4]\n- By retrieving and recalling stored knowledge and memories, the brain helps the agent devise plans, reason about situations, and make informed decisions. [chunk_2]\n- It can also update knowledge and summarize past observations, thoughts, and actions for future use. [chunk_2]",
