      {
        "case_id": "gp005",
        "category": "golden",
        "question": "How does the RAG retriever obtain documents for a query?",
        "answer": "- The RAG retriever uses the DPR bi‑encoder architecture, defining a query encoder q(x) and a document encoder d(z) with pη(z|x) ∝ exp(d(z)ᵀ q(x)) . [chunk_1][chunk_2]\n- Retrieving the top‑k documents is posed as a Maximum Inner Product Search (MIPS) problem, which can be approximated in sub‑linear time . [chunk_1]\n- A pre‑trained DPR bi‑encoder initializes the retriever and builds a document index, referred to as the non‑parametric memory . [chunk_1]\n- During inference the retriever returns the top‑K documents z_i for a query x . [chunk_1]",
